' ARCADE -- Arco Runtime Construction & Application Development Environment.
'
' Phase B (packet Section 34): the minimum shell that can open a project and show four tabs
' (Surface / Flow / Source / Run) sharing one project context. No visual design canvas yet -- per
' the packet's own acceptance criterion, Source is the only functional tab; Surface/Flow/Run show
' an honest "not yet implemented" placeholder rather than a fake preview (packet Section 39.4/39.8
' forbid faking a renderer or hot-reload theater; the same "don't pretend" discipline applies here
' to an empty tab).
'
' See docs/arcade/README.md and docs/ARCADE_PROGRESS.md for the architecture this implements and
' the reasoning behind each decision below.

#IMPORT "arcoui"

' The ARCADE project file format is `.arcoproj` -- a plain ArcoBASIC object-literal expression,
' already real and already loadable via Project.Load (see docs/arcade/README.md's Session 1
' finding 8). Recognized fields: Name, Entry, Files, Window. This loading logic mirrors the
' now-deleted arcoflow.abas prototype's own (proven, working) version of it -- see
' docs/ARCADE_PROGRESS.md for why that prototype was removed; this loading logic specifically was
' worth keeping, since the format itself is an existing convention, not something ARCADE invented.
FUNCTION LoadProject(openedPath)
    project = {}
    project.Name = ""
    project.Root = ""
    project.Entry = ""
    project.Files = []

    projectPath = ""
    IF openedPath <> "" ANDALSO Path.Extension(openedPath) == ".arcoproj" THEN
        projectPath = openedPath
    ELSE
        candidate = Path.Join(Path.DirName(openedPath), "project.arcoproj")
        IF File.Exists(candidate) THEN projectPath = candidate
    END IF

    IF projectPath <> "" THEN
        TRY
            loaded = Project.Load(projectPath)
            project.Name = Object.Get(loaded, "Name", "")
            project.Entry = Object.Get(loaded, "Entry", "")
            project.Root = Path.DirName(projectPath)
            project.Files = Object.Get(loaded, "Files", [])
            ' Deliberately NOT reading the project's own `Window` field here -- that config
            ' describes the size of the WINDOW THE OPENED PROJECT ITSELF WOULD OPEN AT RUNTIME
            ' (see arcade/reference-project/project.arcoproj's own 420x220, sized for Customer
            ' Lookup's own small window, found the hard way: reading it here made ARCADE's OWN
            ' shell open at 420x220 too, cramped enough to clip the fourth tab). ARCADE's own
            ' workspace window size is a separate, ARCADE-level concern -- see WindowWidth/
            ' WindowHeight constants below.
        CATCH err
            PRINT "ARCADE could not load " + projectPath + ": " + err.Message
        END TRY
    END IF

    RETURN project
END FUNCTION

' The four canonical views (packet Section 4). "RUN" stays last in both the tab order and this
' list on purpose -- it is the odd one out (it doesn't show a static representation of the project
' at all, it launches the real thing), matching the packet's own workspace mockup ordering
' (Section 33: "SURFACE FLOW SOURCE RUN").
FUNCTION ViewNames()
    RETURN ["Surface", "Flow", "Source", "Run"]
END FUNCTION

' The content area beneath the tab bar: shows the Source editor when active, an honest "not yet
' implemented" notice for Surface/Flow otherwise, and launches the project's own entry file for
' Run. A single Widget rather than four separately-attached ones because only one is ever visible
' at a time and they share the same bounds -- ArcoSurface has no concept of "hidden" widgets, so
' the alternative (attaching all four and toggling visibility by hand in each Draw/HandleEvent)
' would just move this same branching into ArcadeShell instead of removing it.
CLASS ContentArea IMPLEMENTS Widget
    ActiveTab = "Source"
    SourceEditor = NULL
    EntryPath = ""
    ProjectName = ""
    X = 0
    Y = 0
    Width = 0
    Height = 0
    RunStatus = ""

    CONSTRUCTOR(entryPath, projectName)
        SELF.EntryPath = entryPath
        SELF.ProjectName = projectName
        content = ""
        IF entryPath <> "" ANDALSO File.Exists(entryPath) THEN content = File.ReadText(entryPath)
        SELF.SourceEditor = TextArea(content)
    END CONSTRUCTOR

    FUNCTION SetBounds(x, y, width, height)
        SELF.X = x
        SELF.Y = y
        SELF.Width = width
        SELF.Height = height
        ignored = SELF.SourceEditor.SetBounds(x, y, width, height)
    END FUNCTION

    ' Writes the Source editor's current text back to the entry file. Phase B's acceptance is
    ' "source file can be opened and edited" -- this is the "and saved" half, bound to Ctrl+S
    ' below, the conventional editor shortcut rather than an ARCADE invention.
    FUNCTION SaveSource()
        IF SELF.EntryPath == "" THEN RETURN FALSE
        File.WriteText(SELF.EntryPath, SELF.SourceEditor.Text)
        RETURN TRUE
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION RunProject()
        IF SELF.EntryPath == "" THEN
            SELF.RunStatus = "No entry file to run."
            RETURN
        END IF
        ' Compiled-and-run each time, not "launch a pre-built binary": Run must reflect whatever
        ' is actually on disk right now, including an unsaved-to-Source-but-saved-to-disk edit --
        ' see docs/arcade/runtime-inspection.md's own "no fake hot reload" discipline. This shells
        ' out the same way the deleted arcoflow.abas prototype did (Process.Run -> ArcoFission
        ' compile-run), the one piece of its approach worth keeping as-is.
        arcofission = Process.Env("ARCOFISSION_PATH")
        IF arcofission == "" THEN arcofission = "ArcoFission"
        command = ShellQuoteArcade(arcofission) + " compile-run " + ShellQuoteArcade(SELF.EntryPath)
        result = Process.Run(command)
        SELF.RunStatus = result.Output
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION Draw(window)
        IF SELF.ActiveTab == "Source" THEN
            SELF.SourceEditor.Focused = TRUE
            ignored = SELF.SourceEditor.Draw(window)
        ELSE
            SELF.SourceEditor.Focused = FALSE
            IF SELF.ActiveTab == "Run" THEN
                GUI.Text(window, "Run -- " + SELF.EntryPath, SELF.X, SELF.Y, 16, 0.82, 0.86, 0.90, 1.0)
                GUI.Text(window, "Press R to compile and run through ArcoFission compile-run.", SELF.X, SELF.Y + 26, 13, 0.56, 0.64, 0.66, 1.0)
                IF SELF.RunStatus <> "" THEN
                    GUI.Text(window, SELF.RunStatus, SELF.X, SELF.Y + 56, 13, 0.7, 0.85, 0.75, 1.0)
                END IF
            ELSE
                GUI.Text(window, SELF.ActiveTab + " -- not yet implemented.", SELF.X, SELF.Y, 16, 0.6, 0.65, 0.7, 1.0)
                GUI.Text(window, "See docs/arcade/" + Lower(SELF.ActiveTab) + ".md for direction.", SELF.X, SELF.Y + 26, 13, 0.5, 0.55, 0.58, 1.0)
            END IF
        END IF
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION HandleEvent(window, event)
        changed = FALSE
        IF SELF.ActiveTab == "Source" THEN
            changed = SELF.SourceEditor.HandleEvent(window, event)
            IF event.Type == "key" ANDALSO event.Action == "press" ANDALSO event.Ctrl ANDALSO event.Key == "s" THEN
                ignored = SELF.SaveSource()
            END IF
        END IF
        IF SELF.ActiveTab == "Run" ANDALSO event.Type == "key" ANDALSO event.Action == "press" ANDALSO event.Key == "r" THEN
            ignored = SELF.SaveSource()
            ignored = SELF.RunProject()
        END IF
        RETURN changed
    END FUNCTION
END CLASS

FUNCTION ShellQuoteArcade(text)
    RETURN "'" + String.Replace(text, "'", "'\''") + "'"
END FUNCTION

IF GUI.Available() == FALSE THEN
    PRINT "ARCADE needs a Wayland or X11 desktop session."
ELSE
    TRY
        openedPath = ""
        IF LEN(Args) > 0 THEN openedPath = Args[0]

        project = LoadProject(openedPath)
        entryPath = ""
        IF project.Entry <> "" THEN entryPath = Path.Join(project.Root, project.Entry)

        windowTitle = "ARCADE"
        IF project.Name <> "" THEN windowTitle = "ARCADE -- " + project.Name

        ' ARCADE's own workspace window size -- deliberately independent of whatever window size
        ' the opened project's own app declares for itself (see LoadProject's own comment).
        shellWidth = 1200
        shellHeight = 760

        app = App("ARCADE")
        win = app.Window(windowTitle, shellWidth, shellHeight)

        views = ViewNames()
        content = ContentArea(entryPath, project.Name)

        ' One intent per tab, one Button per tab -- reusing the same, already-proven Button/Widget/
        ' Intent machinery ArcoUI's own examples use for every other click target, rather than
        ' hand-rolling tab-bar hit-testing inside ArcadeShell (packet Section 39.6 forbids a
        ' Surface-specific event system separate from what ArcoBASIC/ArcoUI already provides; the
        ' same discipline applies to ARCADE's own UI, not just to applications ARCADE edits).
        tabX = win.Theme.Spacing
        FOR viewName IN views
            ignored = win.DefineIntent("Show" + viewName)
            tabButton = Button(viewName)
            tabButton.SetBounds(tabX, win.Theme.Spacing, 110, 34)
            ignored = win.Attach(tabButton, "Show" + viewName)
            tabX = tabX + 110 + win.Theme.Spacing
        NEXT

        contentY = win.Theme.Spacing * 2 + 34
        ignored = content.SetBounds(win.Theme.Spacing, contentY, shellWidth - win.Theme.Spacing * 2, shellHeight - contentY - win.Theme.Spacing)
        ignored = win.Attach(content, "", TRUE)

        WHILE app.AnyOpen()
            timestamp = Time.Timestamp()
            event = GUI.WaitEvent(0.02)
            IF event.Type <> "none" THEN
                target = app.SurfaceForWindow(event.Window)
                IF target <> NULL THEN
                    IF event.Type == "close" THEN
                        ignored = target.Invoke("Close", timestamp)
                    ELSE
                        ignored = target.HandleEvent(event, timestamp)
                    END IF
                END IF
            END IF
            ignored = app.Pump()

            tabEvent = app.PollEvent()
            WHILE tabEvent <> NULL
                FOR viewName IN views
                    IF tabEvent.Intent == win.IntentHandle("Show" + viewName) THEN content.ActiveTab = viewName
                NEXT
                tabEvent = app.PollEvent()
            WEND

            FOR surface IN app.Surfaces
                IF NOT surface.ShouldClose() THEN ignored = surface.Draw()
            NEXT
        WEND
        FOR surface IN app.Surfaces
            ignored = surface.Close()
        NEXT
    CATCH err
        PRINT "ARCADE failed: " + err
    END TRY
END IF
